-- title:
--   Monogenic integers in finite extensions inside ℚ̄ₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\,p$ denote the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q_p$ with its norm extending the $p$-adic absolute value. Let $F$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb Q_p \subseteq \mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\,p$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q_p$, and let $E$ be an intermediate field of $F \subseteq \mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\,p$ that is finite-dimensional over $F$. Then there is an element $x$ of $E$ with the following three properties: its norm as an element of $\mathrm{PadicAlgCl}\,p$ satisfies $\|x\| \le 1$; the intermediate field of $F \subseteq E$ generated by $x$ is all of $E$, i.e. $E = F(x)$; and every $y \in E$ with $\|y\| \le 1$ is of the form $y = P(x)$ for some polynomial $P \in \mathbb Q_p[X]$ all of whose coefficients have norm at most $1$, the value $P(x)$ being taken via the $\mathbb Q_p$-algebra structure of $E$. Thus the valuation ring of $E$ is generated over $\mathbb Z_p$ by the single element $x$, which simultaneously generates $E$ over $F$.
--
--   This is the monogenicity of the ring of integers of a finite extension of $\mathbb Q_p$, in the strong form in which one generator works over $\mathbb Z_p$ and at the same time generates the field over any intermediate field $F$; the characterisation of the condition $\|x\| \le 1$ as integrality over $\mathbb Z_p$ is supplied by [`PadicAlgCl.isIntegral_padicInt_iff_norm_le_one`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.isIntegral_padicInt_iff_norm_le_one). It is used in the quantitative study of the cyclotomic tower inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$, namely for the approximation statement [`PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_rpow_neg_lt_norm_algEquiv_sub_of_mem_sup_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_rpow_neg_lt_norm_algEquiv_sub_of_mem_sup_cyclotomicTower) and the bound on trace duals [`PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower).
-- source:
